<node id="reg_nj_ocean_container_permit">
  <data key="d2">NJ Commercial Vehicle Size and Weight Guidebook — 3.4 Ocean Borne Container Permit (Annual)</data>
  <data key="d3">source_clause</data>
  <data key="d4">archive</data>
  <data key="d5">{"rule_id": "reg_nj_ocean_container_permit", "label": "NJ Commercial Vehicle Size and Weight Guidebook — 3.4 Ocean Borne Container Permit (Annual)", "authority_entity_id": "authority_njdot", "source_id": "nj_size_weight_guidebook", "source_locator": "PDF page 43, section 3.4 and Table 5", "source_text": ["An Ocean Borne Container Permit can be obtained for a truck tractor semitrailer combination engaged in the overweight transportation of sealed containers of the type commonly used for the conveyance of freight transportation in international ocean-going commerce. Moves made under this permit type must be of legal dimensions and are subject to the weight limitations shown in Table 5.", "TABLE 5 OCEAN BORNE CONTAINER PERMIT WEIGHT LIMITATIONS: Maximum Gross Weight 90,000 lbs; Maximum Tandem Weight 38,000 lbs; Maximum Tri-axle Weight 56,400 lbs."], "source_text_verbatim": true, "corroborating_source_ids": ["njac_13_18_osow_portal_copy_2026_08_24"], "related_code_sections": ["N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.2(c)", "N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.3(a)(2)"], "keys_on": ["weight", "axle_weights", "dimensions", "container_seal_status", "trip_timing", "permit_credential_status"], "applicability_profile_id": "scoped_80000lb_5axle_nonhaz_inbound_apm", "required_profile_facts": ["gross_weight_lbs", "axle_group_weights_lbs", "width_inches", "height_inches", "overall_length_feet", "container_seal_status", "permit_credential_status", "trip_date_time"], "missing_profile_facts": ["axle_group_weights_lbs", "width_inches", "height_inches", "overall_length_feet", "container_seal_status", "permit_credential_status", "trip_date_time"], "applicability_status": "indeterminate_missing_rule_keyed_facts", "matching_scope_facts": ["vehicle_use=container_drayage", "gross_weight_lbs=80000"], "applicability_note": "The supplied gross weight does not establish legal axle or bridge-formula compliance, and the profile does not state legal dimensions, sealed-container status, permit status, or trip timing.", "compliance_status": "not_a_compliance_claim", "graph_eligibility": "include_as_exact_conditional_rule_scope_unresolved"}</data>
</node>
<node id="reg_nj_osow_permit_requirement_13_18_portal_copy">
  <data key="d2">N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.2 — Requirement of permit (NJPASS-hosted rule copy)</data>
  <data key="d3">source_clause</data>
  <data key="d4">archive</data>
  <data key="d5">{"rule_id": "reg_nj_osow_permit_requirement_13_18_portal_copy", "label": "N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.2 — Requirement of permit (NJPASS-hosted rule copy)", "authority_entity_id": "authority_njmvc", "source_id": "njac_13_18_osow_portal_copy_2026_08_24", "source_locator": "PDF pages 1-2, N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.2(a)-(c)(2)", "source_text": ["(a) Except as provided in (c) below, a single-trip permit is required for each one-way trip of an oversize or overweight vehicle that exceeds the dimension or weight provisions of N.J.S.A. 39:3-84.", "(b) In the event the vehicle is both oversize and overweight, a single-trip permit will be issued for each one-way trip.", "(c) An annual ocean borne containerized cargo multiple-trip permit may be issued for a tractor semitrailer combination engaged in the transportation of sealed containers of the type commonly used for the conveyance of freight transportation in international ocean going commerce as follows:", "1. Sealed containers transported under an annual ocean borne containerized cargo multiple-trip permit shall bear the seal of the United States Custom Service, the seal of another governmental agency or the seal of a shipper;", "2. The combined gross vehicle weight of any tractor semitrailer combination, including load or content conveying sealed containers, shall not exceed 90,000 pounds. The tractor semitrailer combination per-axle combined weight shall not exceed 38,000 pounds for any one tandem axle unit in any tractor semitrailer combination and shall not exceed 56,400 pounds for any tri-axle trailer configuration. Additionally, vehicles shall conform with the axle limitations in N.J.S.A. 39:3-84 and the maximum tire load limit in N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.10(a)2. Vehicles or combination of vehicles that exceed these weight limits may not use an annual ocean borne containerized cargo multiple-trip permit and shall obtain a single-trip permit as described in (a) above;"], "source_text_verbatim": true, "keys_on": ["weight", "axle_weights", "dimensions", "container_seal_status", "permit_credential_status"], "applicability_status": "source_text_verified_current_force_not_fully_verified", "currentness_limit": "The current NJPASS portal serves this rule copy, but its PDF metadata dates to 2010 and the official code of record was not independently archived and compared.", "matching_scope_facts": ["geography=New_Jersey"], "compliance_status": "not_a_compliance_claim", "graph_eligibility": "exclude_currentness_not_fully_verified"}</data>
</node>
<node id="reg_nj_semitrailer_length">
  <data key="d2">NJ Commercial Vehicle Size and Weight Guidebook — 2.1.3.6 Trailers and Semitrailers (N.J.S.A. 39:3-84.a(4))</data>
  <data key="d3">source_clause</data>
  <data key="d4">archive</data>
  <data key="d5">{"rule_id": "reg_nj_semitrailer_length", "label": "NJ Commercial Vehicle Size and Weight Guidebook — 2.1.3.6 Trailers and Semitrailers (N.J.S.A. 39:3-84.a(4))", "authority_entity_id": "authority_njdot", "source_id": "nj_size_weight_guidebook", "source_locator": "PDF page 21, section 2.1.3.6", "source_text": ["As the diagram above shows, the maximum length of a semitrailer shall not exceed 53 feet when operated as part of a combination of vehicles consisting of one motor-drawn vehicle and a drawing or power unit vehicle.", "Semitrailers greater than 48 feet in length but not more than 53 feet in length must be transported using the National Network unless seeking food, fuel, rest, repairs or to reach a terminal by the direct route (that is, the shortest travel distance). Upon completing each trip, the large truck should return to the National Network in a manner consistent with reaching its next terminal. Trips off of the National Network or the New Jersey Access Network onto all other local unrestricted roadways should only be for the purpose of accessing a terminal on those roadways, by the shortest distance."], "source_text_verbatim": true, "keys_on": ["dimensions"], "applicability_status": "confirmed_applicable_to_tractor_semitrailer_combinations_in_new_jersey", "matching_scope_facts": ["configuration=standard_five_axle_tractor_semitrailer", "geography=New_Jersey"], "compliance_status": "not_a_compliance_claim", "graph_eligibility": "include"}</data>
</node>
<node id="reg_nj_single_trip_osow_permit">
  <data key="d2">NJ Commercial Vehicle Size and Weight Guidebook — 3.1 Single-Trip OS/OW Permit</data>
  <data key="d3">source_clause</data>
  <data key="d4">archive</data>
  <data key="d5">{"rule_id": "reg_nj_single_trip_osow_permit", "label": "NJ Commercial Vehicle Size and Weight Guidebook — 3.1 Single-Trip OS/OW Permit", "authority_entity_id": "authority_njdot", "source_id": "nj_size_weight_guidebook", "source_locator": "PDF page 40, section 3.1", "source_text": "A single-trip permit allows a carrier to haul a non-divisible load above legal size and/or weight limitations and is valid for a single trip within a period of five days. In the event the one-way trip cannot be completed within the valid life of the single-trip permit due to hazardous road conditions or vehicle breakdown, a one-day extension may be granted provided that the request is made to the DOT before the permit has expired. Permit restrictions are assigned based on requested dimensions and weights.", "source_text_verbatim": true, "corroborating_source_ids": ["njac_13_18_osow_portal_copy_2026_08_24"], "related_code_sections": ["N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.2(a)", "N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.3(a)(1) and (b)", "N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.6"], "keys_on": ["weight", "axle_weights", "axle_spacings", "dimensions", "load_divisibility", "trip_timing", "permit_credential_status"], "applicability_profile_id": "scoped_80000lb_5axle_nonhaz_inbound_apm", "required_profile_facts": ["gross_weight_lbs", "axle_weights_lbs", "axle_spacings_inches", "width_inches", "height_inches", "overall_length_feet", "load_divisibility_status", "permit_credential_status", "trip_date_time"], "missing_profile_facts": ["axle_weights_lbs", "axle_spacings_inches", "width_inches", "height_inches", "overall_length_feet", "load_divisibility_status", "permit_credential_status", "trip_date_time"], "applicability_status": "indeterminate_missing_rule_keyed_facts", "matching_scope_facts": ["gross_weight_lbs=80000"], "applicability_note": "The gross weight is supplied, but the guidebook's bridge-formula note states that legal gross weight may be below 80,000 pounds depending on axle weights and spacing. Missing dimensions, load divisibility, permit status, and trip timing also prevent a permit determination.", "compliance_status": "not_a_compliance_claim", "graph_eligibility": "include_as_exact_conditional_rule_scope_unresolved"}</data>
</node>
<node id="reg_nj_single_trip_route_review_13_18_portal_copy">
  <data key="d2">N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.5 — Permit applications and route review (NJPASS-hosted rule copy)</data>
  <data key="d3">source_clause</data>
  <data key="d4">archive</data>
  <data key="d5">{"rule_id": "reg_nj_single_trip_route_review_13_18_portal_copy", "label": "N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.5 — Permit applications and route review (NJPASS-hosted rule copy)", "authority_entity_id": "authority_njmvc", "source_id": "njac_13_18_osow_portal_copy_2026_08_24", "source_locator": "PDF pages 3-4, N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.5(b)(3)-(7), (d), and (e)", "source_text": ["3. The vehicle height, length and width;", "4. The axle configuration and weight over each axle;", "5. The overall gross vehicle weight;", "6. The dates of travel;", "7. The details of the anticipated route of travel, including locations of the entrance to and exit from the New Jersey State highway system, including, but not limited to, the interstate highways, the New Jersey Turnpike, the Garden State Parkway south of Exit 105 and the Atlantic City Expressway; and", "(d) Applications for single-trip permits will be reviewed for acceptability of the route being used in conjunction with the vehicle's load and axle configuration.", "(e) Applications for single-trip permits will be rejected where the vehicle's load and axle configuration overstress the structures being crossed on the anticipated route of travel. Rejected applications will identify the structures on the proposed route being overstressed. Applicants can either modify the vehicle's load, weight over each axle or axle spacing to lessen the load impact or choose an alternative route. Applicants can contact the New Jersey Department of Transportation, Bureau of Structural Engineering at 609-530-2579 for assistance in the choice of acceptable alternative routes."], "source_text_verbatim": true, "keys_on": ["weight", "axle_weights", "axle_spacings", "dimensions", "trip_timing", "route_geometry", "permit_credential_status"], "applicability_status": "source_text_verified_current_force_not_fully_verified", "currentness_limit": "The current NJPASS portal serves this rule copy, but the official code of record was not independently archived and compared.", "matching_scope_facts": ["geography=New_Jersey"], "compliance_status": "not_a_compliance_claim", "graph_eligibility": "exclude_currentness_not_fully_verified"}</data>
</node>
<node id="reg_nj_tandem_gross_bridge">
  <data key="d2">NJ Commercial Vehicle Size and Weight Guidebook — 2.2.2 Groups of Two or More Axles</data>
  <data key="d3">source_clause</data>
  <data key="d4">archive</data>
  <data key="d5">{"rule_id": "reg_nj_tandem_gross_bridge", "label": "NJ Commercial Vehicle Size and Weight Guidebook — 2.2.2 Groups of Two or More Axles", "authority_entity_id": "authority_njdot", "source_id": "nj_size_weight_guidebook", "source_locator": "PDF pages 28-29; sections 2.2.2, 2.2.2.1, and 2.2.2.2", "source_text": ["The maximum weight allowed on axle group of this type is 34,000 lbs.", "The gross vehicle weight is defined as a vehicle or combination of vehicles, including load or contents. The maximum overall gross weight of a vehicle is 80,000 lbs., as shown in the diagram above.", "NOTE: Compliance with bridge formula weight limits may require axle weights lower than the standard weight limits of 34,000 pounds for a tandem axle set and a gross weight lower than the standard 80,000-pound limit."], "source_text_verbatim": true, "keys_on": ["weight", "axles"], "applicability_status": "confirmed_applicable", "matching_scope_facts": ["gross_weight_lbs=80000", "axle_count=5", "geography=New_Jersey"], "compliance_status": "not_a_compliance_claim", "graph_eligibility": "include"}</data>
</node>
<node id="reg_nj_terminal_access_102_inch_standard_truck">
  <data key="d2">N.J.A.C. 16:32-1.5(a)(2) — Reasonable access to terminals</data>
  <data key="d3">source_clause</data>
  <data key="d4">archive</data>
  <data key="d5">{"rule_id": "reg_nj_terminal_access_102_inch_standard_truck", "label": "N.J.A.C. 16:32-1.5(a)(2) — Reasonable access to terminals", "authority_entity_id": "authority_njdot", "source_id": "njac_16_32_truck_access_current_2023", "source_locator": "PDF pages 3-4, N.J.A.C. 16:32-1.5(a)(2)", "source_text": "A 102-inch-wide standard truck may use local unrestricted roadways only as necessary to: i. Access a terminal located on a local unrestricted roadway, but must return to the National Network or New Jersey Access Network by the direct route unless continued use of the local unrestricted roadway provides the direct route to the next terminal located on a local unrestricted roadway; or ii. Reach the New Jersey Access Network from the National Network by the direct route or to access the National Network from the New Jersey Access Network by the direct route; and", "source_text_verbatim": true, "keys_on": ["dimensions"], "applicability_status": "confirmed_applicable_only_to_102_inch_wide_standard_trucks", "matching_scope_facts": ["rule_vehicle_scope=102-inch-wide_standard_truck"], "compliance_status": "not_a_compliance_claim", "graph_eligibility": "include_as_exact_conditional_rule"}</data>
</node>
<node id="reg_nj_toll_authority_approval_13_18_portal_copy">
  <data key="d2">N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.9(a)(2) — Toll-road approval (NJPASS-hosted rule copy)</data>
  <data key="d3">source_clause</data>
  <data key="d4">archive</data>
  <data key="d5">{"rule_id": "reg_nj_toll_authority_approval_13_18_portal_copy", "label": "N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.9(a)(2) — Toll-road approval (NJPASS-hosted rule copy)", "authority_entity_id": "authority_njmvc", "source_id": "njac_13_18_osow_portal_copy_2026_08_24", "source_locator": "PDF page 5, N.J.A.C. 13:18-1.9(a)(2)", "source_text": "2. On any toll road, without the express approval of the tolling authority, including, but not limited to, the South Jersey Transportation Authority for the Atlantic City Expressway; and the New Jersey Turnpike Authority for the New Jersey Turnpike and the Garden State Parkway;", "source_text_verbatim": true, "keys_on": ["route_geometry", "permit_credential_status"], "applicability_status": "source_text_verified_current_force_not_fully_verified", "currentness_limit": "The current NJPASS portal serves this rule copy, but the official code of record was not independently archived and compared.", "matching_scope_facts": ["path_a_uses_new_jersey_turnpike_approach"], "compliance_status": "not_a_compliance_claim", "graph_eligibility": "exclude_currentness_not_fully_verified"}</data>
